WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.864
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Wednesday, October twenty eighth.

2
00:00:04.864 --> 00:00:12.562
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.562 --> 00:00:15.643
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:15.643 --> 00:00:17.084
We start in Serbia.

5
00:00:17.084 --> 00:00:24.607
The Associated Press reports an assailant attacked a guard with knives outside the Israeli Embassy in Belgrade overnight and was killed, Serbian police said.

6
00:00:24.607 --> 00:00:29.529
Interior Minister Ivica Dacic said police were treating it as a terrorist attack.

7
00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:32.683
The Times of Israel reports the attacker was a minor.

8
00:00:32.683 --> 00:00:38.554
TRAC describes him as a teenage Islamic State supporter.

9
00:00:38.554 --> 00:00:48.486
On the Pakistan and Afghanistan border, Dawn reports Afghan security forces opened fire on Pakistan Army border posts and residential areas in the Angoor Adda area of South Waziristan on Tuesday.

10
00:00:48.486 --> 00:00:53.353
Global Decipher reports the clashes later stopped, according to local sources.

11
00:00:53.353 --> 00:01:02.362
In southeastern Iran, Iran International reports gunmen attacked police facilities in Khash, in Sistan and Baluchestan Province, on Tuesday.

12
00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:06.980
Citing a local rights group, it reports several security personnel were killed.

13
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:17.960
In Nigeria, BBC Africa reports a controversial Islamic cleric, Sheikh Yahya Masusuka, was killed outside his home in Katsina State on Monday, October twenty sixth, as he was saying goodbye to visitors.

14
00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:23.544
TRAC attributes the killing to the militant group Ansaru.

15
00:01:23.544 --> 00:01:26.643
Several governments updated Ebola travel guidance.

16
00:01:26.643 --> 00:01:27.143
The U.S.

17
00:01:27.143 --> 00:01:35.195
State Department says Nigeria has reactivated Ebola screening for all international travelers at its air, land and sea ports of entry, including possible quarantine.

18
00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:45.757
Australia's Smartraveller says the Seychelles has introduced entry restrictions for travelers who were recently in the Democratic Republic of the Congo.

19
00:01:45.757 --> 00:01:46.257
The U.K.

20
00:01:46.257 --> 00:01:56.555
Foreign Office updated its Uganda advice with precautionary measures around the outbreak, and its El Salvador advice with Ebola-related quarantine requirements for some travelers.

21
00:01:56.555 --> 00:01:58.744
Now a few quick notes by region.

22
00:01:58.744 --> 00:02:08.678
In the Middle East, Syria's state news agency said passenger and freight traffic through the Nassib crossing with Jordan would resume Wednesday morning, after Tuesday's closure.

23
00:02:08.678 --> 00:02:17.631
Reuters reports Jordan says its strikes in Syria killed more than twenty Islamic State militants, and that Jordan and Syria will form a joint security committee.

24
00:02:17.631 --> 00:02:23.408
Reuters also reports the Houthis say they hit Saudi Arabia's Ras Tanura refinery with a missile.

25
00:02:23.408 --> 00:02:27.360
The Institute for the Study of War says it cannot verify that claim.

26
00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:27.860
The U.K.

27
00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:36.564
Foreign Office updated its travel advice for more than a dozen countries across the region, with new information on regional tensions.

28
00:02:36.564 --> 00:02:48.259
In Africa, News Central Television reports Nigeria's emergency management agency now says at least sixty two people were killed in Friday's attack in Taraba State, with fifty two injured and thousands displaced.

29
00:02:48.259 --> 00:02:56.672
In Ethiopia, the Critical Threats Project reports federal forces captured a senior Tigray People's Liberation Front commander in central Tigray.

30
00:02:56.672 --> 00:03:06.195
In South Asia, Reuters reports Cyclone Arnab made landfall on India's east coast, uprooting trees and electricity poles as thousands took shelter.

31
00:03:06.195 --> 00:03:12.533
Canada's travel advisory service told Canadians in India to check its advice often as the storm moves.

32
00:03:12.533 --> 00:03:13.033
The U.S.

33
00:03:13.033 --> 00:03:22.754
State Department says Nepal's weather authorities have warned of heavy rain, strong winds and heavy snowfall in parts of the country from October twenty ninth to thirty first.

34
00:03:22.754 --> 00:03:30.321
In Europe, Reuters reports France has temporarily sent a maritime patrol plane to the Black Sea after attacks on cargo ships.

35
00:03:30.321 --> 00:03:39.058
The Record reports Russian authorities are limiting internet access as leaders from Iran, Venezuela and several African countries arrive for summits.

36
00:03:39.058 --> 00:03:46.975
In the Americas, Reuters reports the U.S. military says five people were killed in its latest strike on a vessel in the Eastern Pacific.

37
00:03:46.975 --> 00:04:01.047
And in cyber, Reuters reports, citing researchers at TrendAI, that the Israeli company Discover-Tech was one of the biggest sources of digital ads shown to Starlink users, and that the ads were likely used to geolocate or surveil them.

38
00:04:01.047 --> 00:04:02.474
That's today's brief.

39
00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:10.701
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

40
00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:18.984
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

41
00:04:18.984 --> 00:04:21.150
This brief is digitally narrated.

42
00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.098
Questions?

43
00:04:22.098 --> 00:04:25.634
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

44
00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:27.601
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
